      "mira_version": "ae03a3877912",
      "prompt_version": "hub-chat:machine_selected",
      "retrieval_version": "oem_corpus_bm25",
      "answer_text": "\u26a0\ufe0f No page of the Allen-Bradley SLC 5/03 manual matched this question. The closest match is a related manual (Rockwell Automation CompactLogix, Rockwell Automation ControlLogix). Anything taken from it may differ on your SLC 5/03 \u2014 confirm them in your SLC 5/03 manual before you act.\n\nThe PLC stops communicating because the USR\u2011N540 is a transparent RS\u2011485\u2011to\u2011Ethernet converter that does not implement the DH\u2011485 protocol the SLC\u202f5/03 expects, so the controller receives raw RS\u2011485 data that it cannot interpret [1].\n\nWith the PLC locked out and the DH\u2011485 bus de\u2011energized, check that the RS\u2011485 wiring (including proper termination) matches the DH\u2011485 half\u2011duplex specifications and verify that the converter is configured (or capable) to speak the DH\u2011485 protocol before reconnecting the network [1].",
      "answer_status": "answered",
      "citations": [
